{"labs": [{"id": 0, "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn8le12ob03re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "Cindy Jones has become the oldest person in the world this year. She has enjoyed eating bacon for over a hundred years. Jones is now in her 116th year.  At 115 years old, she has been verified as one of two people still alive who were born in the 19th century.  Cindy is a supercentenarian \u2014 a person who has lived beyond 110 years. Today, surprisingly, there are around 30 supercentenarians among us. Even though Jones' accomplishment of longevity isn't unparalleled, her  bill of health, which is almost perfect, has amazed medical professionals. To try and discover how I might live to be a supercentenarian, I interviewed Jones.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn8le12ob03re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "From the beginning, Cindy has led a simple life: no parties, smoking, alcohol or drugs. Her daily regimen is uncomplicated.  With a glass of water every morning, she is supposed to take her blood-pressure medication and a multivitamin. She is supposed to see the doctor every 3 months for \"maintenance\". Cindy's diet consists largely of fruit. To the bewilderment of her physicians, Jones has even appeared to be \"reverse aging.\" During the past four years, her hair has not only become softer but has changed back from gray to brown.", "id": 2, "time": "47000", "image": "engenn8le12ob03re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "The question is: How are we supposed to achieve longevity like Cindy? Does diet and lifestyle contribute to living longer, or is it a genetic lottery?\nThough the research remains inconclusive,  it has suggested that people, like Cindy, who live beyond a 100 years have a complicated genetic makeup that helps them avoid getting age-related diseases.", "id": 3, "time": "85000", "image": "engenn8le12ob03re2img03.jpg"}], "audiosrc": "engenn8le12ob03re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn8le12ob03re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "_data": [], "type": "audio", "template_override": 1}], "exercises": [{"id": 0, "type": "WLC", "questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about people's habits and about staying healthy.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about things I have done or things that have happened.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about things I am supposed to do and things that are supposed to happen.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " How old do you think the world's oldest person is?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " Would you want to live to the age of 100? Why or why not?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "The world's oldest person!", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1}, {"id": 1, "stimuli_ids": [1], "questions": [{"_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}], "responses": [{"id": 0, "selected": 0, "correct": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, {"id": 1, "selected": 0, "correct": 1, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " Let's read about Cindy Jones - the oldest person in the world! Is \u201c<span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">reverse aging</span>\u201d possible?", "type": "tex